(A copy of a list that has been freed is an empty list of its own, and an
 append to it works; the freed list itself still refuses one.)
a list called xs is ["a"].
Free xs.
a list called ys is xs.
append "b" to ys.
On error print "append to the copy refused".
Print "ys: {ys}".
a list called zs is [1].
Free zs.
append "c" to zs.
On error print "append to the freed list refused".
Print "zs: {zs}".
